          "description": {
            "comment": "Metagenomic studies of the geothermal soils of the Favara Grande, Pantelleria, Italy, resulted in a near complete metagenome assembled genomes (MAG) of an aerobic methanotroh, which was classified as Methylobacter. In this study, this Methylobacter sp. B2 is analyzed phylogenetically and its metabolic potential is investigated. The MAG has a size of 4,086,539 bp, consists of 134 contigs and 3955 genes are found, of which 3902 are protein coding genes. All genes for CH4 oxidation were detected, except for formaldehyde dehydrogenase. Formaldehyde to formate conversion is likely to go via the tetrahydromethanopterin (H4MPT) pathway. Methylobacter sp. B2 uses the Ribulose Mono Phosphate (RuMP) pathway for carbon fixation",
            "organism": {
              "organism_name": "Candidatus Methylobacter favarea",
              "tax_id": 2707345
            },
            "title": "Draft genome of a novel methanotrophic Methylobacter sp. from the volcanic soils of Pantelleria Island"
